eldon ring's millennia has changed again  ps5 finally has variable refresh rate  and more  in a previous patch elden ring's hardest  boss fight millennia was accidentally  made more difficult that patch let her  regain health from attacks even when she  made contact with nothing but air given  her two phases and ability to kill you  with just one good string of attacks  this made the fight borderline  impossible thankfully fromsoft has  remedied the situation according to the  1.04 patch notes the new update fixed a  bug with millennia in which her hp was  not healed correctly in the online  multiplayer environment i still haven't  gotten to her yet in my playthrough but  this is pretty good to hear and i also  hope let me solo her still active once i  do get to that point other changes  include a vague fix for a bug that  caused some bosses to die at unintended  times meaning our days of cheesing could  be coming to an end but fingers crossed  that they're not completely over yet and  in other update news or lack thereof  ps5s now have variable refresh rate  support earlier this week sony announced  that vrr support would be coming to the  playstation 5 through a new firmware  update but it seems this feature is  already waiting to be used on your  console many users have found that vrr  is in fact already available on the ps5  presumably added to the console via the  previous update but kept deactivated  until now a simple reboot of your ps5  should let you access the feature via  the playstation 5's display settings  menu allowing you to enable it if you  have the console connected to a  supported display by default vrr is  enabled only for games that officially  support it with sony releasing a list of  games like miles morales and ratchet and  clink rift apart that have already  received patches to work with the  feature you can also enable a toggle  that lets vrr be used at a system level  and apply to all games although sony  warns that its performance might vary or  not appear at all on a game by game  basis and while we're on the subject of  playstation the ps plus leak was correct  and starting may 3rd subscribers can  grab fifa 22 curse of the dead gods and  tribes of midgard for free so mark your  calendars but wait the update news  doesn't stop there grand theft auto 5 on  ps5 and series xns has added some  welcome updates which while seemingly  minor go a long way in improving the  nearly decade old game the biggest  change is a new motion blur slider  allowing players to tone down or  completely turn off motion blur making  car gameplay look more crisp and  detailed the ability to customize the  game's motion blur is something that  fans have requested since the new  versions launched with the effect  becoming way more intrusive at higher  frame rates the update also fixed the  bug on xbox where in-game music would be  muted when players were in an xbox live  party as well as a handful of other  issues affecting audio on the xbox  players have also reported finding new  improvements including new options for  displaying and hiding activities on the  map and fix shadows on new gen xbox  consoles players have also discovered  that the new gen update files are also  present on pc though are currently empty  suggesting that the update will come to  pc at some point in the near future so  do you like to play your games with  motion blur on or off let me know in the  comments below and then head over to  twitter and wish my internet father greg  miller a happy birthday he turns 21  today and it's pretty cool that he  finally gets to drink legally i'll see  you tomorrow  [Music]
 

